# local verification artifacts (screenshots + throwaway drivers)
#
# THE LEADING UNDERSCORE IS THE CONVENTION for a throwaway driver — a script written to drive the
# browser, probe the chain or measure one thing, and then deleted. `shot.tmp.mjs` was the old
# hand-maintained spelling and it only ever covered the one name somebody remembered.
#
# It stopped being theoretical on 2026-08-22: three agents' probe scripts and one of mine were
# committed to main because the ignore list named a file rather than a shape. A convention that
# depends on remembering is not a convention.
_*.mjs
_*.sql
_*.ts
shot.tmp.mjs
*.png
supabase/.temp/
scripts/.bbox-table.txt
